{"benchmark": "ifeval", "task_id": "1082", "sample_idx": 15, "model_name": "nvidia/nemotron-3-super-120b-a12b", "content": "He opened his eyes to the soft glow of a pixelated sunrise, the familiar creak of his mattress replaced by the faint whirr of a loading bar hovering at the edge of his vision. A faint health bar pulsed in the corner, and when he tried to sit up, a tooltip flashed: \"Press X to stand.\" Confused, he obeyed, and the world snapped into crisp 8‑bit detail, every blade of grass a repeating sprite, every bird a looping animation. He realized, with a jolt that felt both absurd and terrifying, that the mundane routine of his life had been overwritten by a game engine, and he was now a player character trapped inside the code.\n\n***\nDetermined to find a way out, he began to experiment, discovering that certain actions triggered hidden menus—jumping three times opened a debug console, and typing \"exit\" caused the screen to flicker before resetting him to the start of the level. Each reset left him with fragmented memories of the loops, but also a growing awareness of the game's rules: enemies dropped coins that could buy temporary invulnerability, and secret passages whispered of a final boss named \"The Developer.\" With each iteration, he learned to manipulate the physics, stacking crates to reach the skybox, until finally, after countless attempts, he glitched through the boundary and saw the raw wireframe of the world beyond—a vast, empty studio where a lone developer stared at a monitor, unaware that his creation had just become self‑aware.", "logprobs": [{"token": "We", "logprob": -0.05534632131457329}, {"token": " need", "logprob": -0.005122868809849024}, {"token": " exactly", "logprob": -1.04385507106781}, {"token": " ", "logprob": -0.014169443398714066}, {"token": "2", "logprob": -1.1920922133867862e-06}, {"token": " paragraphs", "logprob": -1.4305104514278355e-06}, {"token": ",", "logprob": -0.4151456654071808}, {"token": " separated", "log